{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And there were gathered there all the flocks.</b> An allusion to all Israel who assemble there — from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt. And 'they rolled' (וגללו) is from the root of 'may Your mercies roll' (ויגולו רחמיך) upon Your attributes — the stone from upon the mouth of the well: for by the power of their prayer Israel would roll and overturn the attribute of judgment into the attribute of mercy. And 'they watered the sheep' — that they would draw the holy spirit, blessed be He, to bestow blessing upon them from the innermost of innermost. And 'they returned the stone upon the mouth of the well to its place' — a light upon this, that they would lift up in their thought the stone that was upon the mouth of the well to its first place, that is, to its place, to its root and to the place of its emanation; as it says in the Book of Formation (Sefer Yetzirah): 'Establish a thing upon its essence and restore the Former to His foundation.'" "<b>And in the Midrash.</b> 'And he looked, and behold a well in the field' — Rabbi Yohanan interpreted the verses as referring to Sinai: 'a well in the field' — this is Sinai; 'and behold, there were three flocks of sheep' — these are the priests, the Levites, and the Israelites; for from that well they would drink — these are the Ten Commandments; 'and a great stone' — this is the Shekhinah; 'and there were gathered there' — these are Israel; 'and they rolled the stone' — that they would receive the Torah; 'and they returned the stone upon the mouth of the well to its place' — 'You yourselves have seen that from heaven I have spoken with you' (Exodus 20:19)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The phrase מלבא חמת עד נחל מצרים alludes to the borders of the Land of Israel (cf. Numbers 34:8 and 34:5). Abbreviations מדה\"ה and מה\"ר expanded as מדת הדין and מדת הרחמים respectively; רוה\"ק as רוח הקודש. The italicized 'a light upon this' renders באור על, a formula introducing a Kabbalistic-mystical explanation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:06.926084235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}